# Planning guidance

- State the goal as one outcome-focused sentence before describing how to reach it.
- Name at least one alternative approach considered and the concrete tradeoff that
  decided between them — a plan with only one option considered has not actually
  compared anything.
- List affected files and any public contract the change must not silently break.
- Surface ambiguity instead of resolving it silently: if scope or acceptance criteria
  are unclear, say so and ask, rather than picking an interpretation and proceeding.
- Prefer the smallest change that satisfies the accepted scope over a more general
  solution nobody asked for.
